WEBVTT

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:15.760
Don't miss that brightly shining light!

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:20.870
It's always there beside you.

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:26.420
I'm sure the rest just depends on your perception.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:31.590
You don't have to search for it—just notice that it's there!

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:37.350
There's a tenderness that lies hidden behind the most common things:

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:43.230
a light that showers our days in color!

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:49.230
Tiny Days: This world is constructed...

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:54.800
Tiny Days: ...by fragments of miracles!

00:00:54.800 --> 00:01:00.180
Things that seemed meaningless

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:05.730
were actually protecting us, loving us, more than we ever knew.

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:10.960
Tiny Heart: Our feelings flow forth...

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:16.000
Tiny Heart: ...as we give thanks for everything we've been given.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:21.490
We'll never, ever forget...

00:01:21.490 --> 00:01:27.700
We'll cherish this feeling forevermore!

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:34.990
Gourai

00:02:19.970 --> 00:02:21.670
Did Papa send me something again?

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:37.680
Swipe for Home Screen
Kotobuki
Bukiko
Incoming
Call

00:02:39.770 --> 00:02:40.660
Bukiko?

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:42.020
'Morning and stuff!

00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:42.980
'Morning.

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:47.190
So, my father all of a sudden is, like, "I want to go for a family drive,"

00:02:47.190 --> 00:02:49.570
and he's making a big scene and stuff...

00:02:49.570 --> 00:02:52.360
I've gotta bail on today's plans. Forgive me?

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:54.410
Sure. No problem.

00:02:54.410 --> 00:02:56.160
Phew, thanks a lot!

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:58.220
I am in your debt, Madam!

00:02:58.220 --> 00:03:01.720
Oh, and I'll totally help you with English on Monday, so get your study on, okay?

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:04.830
Really? Thanks! Well, see you.

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:08.340
Suddenly, I've got nothing to do.

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:11.080
I'm sure not in the mood for English, though.

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:11.920
I mean...

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:14.420
Sunday is just getting started!

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:18.180
Oh, yeah! I forgot.

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:28.110
"Gou... Rai"?

00:03:29.190 --> 00:03:32.600
I'm sure it's a present from Papa to congratulate me on getting into my school.

00:03:35.990 --> 00:03:36.980
A toy?

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:39.610
What is this? What do you do with it?

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:46.080
Huh?

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:52.080
I am Gourai. I have now been activated.

00:03:55.010 --> 00:03:58.640
Wait, what?! Toys these days are awesome!

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:00.340
This thing totally just spoke!

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:03.940
Wow... And this material is a lot softer than I'd expected.

00:04:03.940 --> 00:04:05.380
Master!

00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:05.600
Wow... And this material is a lot softer than I'd expected.

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:07.680
Please stop that, Master.

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:11.070
"Master"? What's that about? That's just weird.

00:04:11.070 --> 00:04:12.950
Then how should I address you?

00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:15.730
I'm Ao. Just call me "Ao."

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:17.730
Understood, Ao.

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:20.410
It sounds so real!

00:04:20.410 --> 00:04:21.690
This doll sure is great.

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:24.700
I wonder where Papa bought it...

00:04:24.870 --> 00:04:27.330
Still, I'm in high school now.

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:29.880
Papa always treats me like a kid!

00:04:30.130 --> 00:04:32.710
Well, I should still send him a thank you message.

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:35.010
Um, Ao?

00:04:35.010 --> 00:04:36.390
Yeah? What?

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:38.540
Please assemble my armor components.

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:39.960
Armor?

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:45.220
I would like you to remove these,
assemble them, and attach them to my body.

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:47.270
Ehh, that sounds like too much work.

00:04:47.270 --> 00:04:50.020
I'm no good at that kind of stuff.

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:51.730
But without these parts, I-

00:04:51.730 --> 00:04:54.100
You're fine the way you are. You're cute!

00:04:55.030 --> 00:04:56.060
Cute?

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:57.160
Yup, that's right!

00:04:57.160 --> 00:04:58.240
"Cute..."

00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:00.950
Anyway, first things first: we should charge you.

00:05:00.950 --> 00:05:01.980
Ah, yes.

00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:04.490
This is your charger, huh?

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:06.570
So, where do I plug this in?

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:09.330
My lower back.

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:10.710
Here, huh?

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:14.770
F.A. Girl.

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:21.140
Um...

00:05:21.140 --> 00:05:21.900
Yeah?

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:24.600
I would like you to attach those parts to me after all.

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:25.420
Huh?

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:32.440
Assembling and equipping them is what will finally make me a Frame Arms Girl.

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:34.690
"Frame Arms Girl"?

00:05:34.690 --> 00:05:37.200
Wait, Gourai-chan, you're not a doll?

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:40.440
No. I am an AS-equipped robot.

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:41.440
"AS"?

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:46.120
It stands for Artificial Self.

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:51.620
I am installed with the intelligence of a 10-year-old human,

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:56.380
but in interacting with you, Master, I am able to learn new information.

00:05:56.380 --> 00:05:58.330
What do you mean, "information"?

00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:00.430
I've heard it's called "emotion."

00:06:00.430 --> 00:06:01.510
Emotion?

00:06:01.510 --> 00:06:02.340
Yes.

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:03.890
Huh...

00:06:03.890 --> 00:06:06.310
So, like, you <i>have</i> to put this stuff on?

00:06:06.310 --> 00:06:07.180
Yes.

00:06:07.180 --> 00:06:08.440
And that's that?

00:06:08.440 --> 00:06:09.980
That is that.

00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:13.140
Well, fine. I guess we can try.

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:15.890
Thank you very much, Ao.

00:06:16.150 --> 00:06:18.280
I can just pop these out, right?

00:06:18.280 --> 00:06:19.030
Stop.

00:06:19.030 --> 00:06:19.530
Huh?

00:06:19.530 --> 00:06:21.280
Please use nippers.

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:22.400
"Nippers"?

00:06:22.660 --> 00:06:23.830
It is a tool.

00:06:23.830 --> 00:06:25.150
Like this.

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:27.290
Oh, those!

00:06:27.290 --> 00:06:29.530
I think the building manager has some.

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:33.160
So, you <i>really</i> have to attach those parts?

00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:38.160
He had some!

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:39.420
These, right?

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:42.080
Th-Those are Kotobuki Nippers!

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:43.390
Huh? What's that?

00:06:43.390 --> 00:06:47.260
They are legendary, said to be nippers of the highest quality.

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:50.020
Their edge is as keen as the finest Japanese steel,

00:06:50.020 --> 00:06:53.310
and the slightest pressure is enough to slice through model parts.

00:06:53.310 --> 00:06:55.270
Edges are cut smooth and flat,

00:06:55.270 --> 00:06:59.140
such that parts almost never turn white, as with normal nippers.

00:06:59.360 --> 00:07:02.490
They were made by a master craftsman from an area known for its blades,

00:07:02.490 --> 00:07:07.160
and their single-edged construction is the perfect balance of cutting edge and required tensile strength.

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:11.080
By having only a single sharp blade, the other end acts as a cutting board,

00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:12.540
meaning parts that are cut free are...

00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:13.290
Stop!

00:07:13.290 --> 00:07:13.950
Again?

00:07:14.380 --> 00:07:19.510
Please remove parts in the order listed in the instruction manual before assembling.

00:07:19.510 --> 00:07:21.000
Oh, really?

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:23.260
Ao, that is No. 6.

00:07:23.260 --> 00:07:24.780
Huh? It's 9, right?

00:07:26.560 --> 00:07:28.560
The underline indicates the correct reading.

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:30.340
This is 9.

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:31.970
Whoa, that was close!

00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:33.970
Ao, stop.

00:07:33.970 --> 00:07:35.480
Now what?

00:07:35.480 --> 00:07:39.780
Please insert Part C9 before snapping those two together.

00:07:41.030 --> 00:07:44.410
If you forget that, you'll have to reassemble it...

00:07:44.410 --> 00:07:48.830
but if you try to take it apart, you run the danger of breaking it.

00:07:48.830 --> 00:07:50.360
That makes sense.

00:08:05.180 --> 00:08:06.050
Ah!

00:08:12.020 --> 00:08:13.660
I can't find it.

00:08:13.660 --> 00:08:14.430
Well, that's fine.

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:16.010
No, it is not.

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:19.020
Huh? Where's the harm? It was just a small part, anyway.

00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:20.650
Let's look a little longer.

00:08:20.650 --> 00:08:21.850
Whaaaaat?

00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:26.410
Ao.

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:30.030
There's something behind here.

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:32.750
It's the photo album my grandma sent me!

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:37.830
Who are these people?

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:40.170
It's me when I was young, Papa, and Mama.

00:08:40.170 --> 00:08:43.210
You live here with your parents?

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:44.780
No, no way.

00:08:44.780 --> 00:08:47.720
Mama and Papa are overseas for his work.

00:08:47.720 --> 00:08:51.560
I'm in high school now, so I'm living on my own.

00:08:51.560 --> 00:08:53.730
I see. Um...

00:08:54.850 --> 00:08:56.760
What's happening here?

00:08:57.150 --> 00:08:58.560
This is...

00:08:58.560 --> 00:09:00.900
Oh. I'm crying because I got stung by a bee.

00:09:00.900 --> 00:09:02.020
Crying...

00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:03.490
And here?

00:09:03.490 --> 00:09:07.320
Well... I think I'm cranky because I dropped my ice cream.

00:09:07.700 --> 00:09:09.020
Cranky...

00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:10.780
What about this?

00:09:10.780 --> 00:09:12.490
This is...

00:09:12.490 --> 00:09:14.120
What <i>is</i> this? I'm smiling, though.

00:09:14.120 --> 00:09:15.530
Smiling...

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:18.280
Why are you smiling?

00:09:18.280 --> 00:09:21.040
Well, I don't know. I don't remember.

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:24.910
Then what sort of emotion does your expression indicate?

00:09:28.050 --> 00:09:29.420
Okay, that's enough.

00:09:29.420 --> 00:09:30.640
But why?

00:09:30.640 --> 00:09:32.720
You ask too many questions. It's a pain.

00:09:33.470 --> 00:09:35.480
I swear, Gourai, you're just like...

00:09:37.310 --> 00:09:38.690
Like...

00:09:38.690 --> 00:09:41.900
Huh? This feels like déjà vu.

00:09:43.190 --> 00:09:44.180
Wait, what?!

00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:47.740
It's night already? So that's why I've been feeling hungry!

00:09:47.740 --> 00:09:48.900
I'll be back soon.

00:09:54.370 --> 00:09:56.790
It seems it got stuck in your clothing.

00:09:57.950 --> 00:09:58.870
Inageya

00:09:58.870 --> 00:09:59.950
Cheep, cheep.
Inageya

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:03.130
Tachikawa Iseya
Sweets

00:10:03.130 --> 00:10:04.420
Welcome!

00:10:04.420 --> 00:10:04.700
Tachikawa Iseya
Sweets

00:10:08.800 --> 00:10:10.240
Crying...

00:10:10.240 --> 00:10:11.700
Cranky...

00:10:11.700 --> 00:10:12.930
Smiling...

00:10:21.810 --> 00:10:23.230
I'm back!

00:10:24.110 --> 00:10:25.650
I remember now, Gourai.

00:10:25.650 --> 00:10:28.890
That déjà vu thing was from when I was a kid.

00:10:30.450 --> 00:10:37.700
When I was young, I looked at a photo album with my Mama and was like, "What's this?" "What's that?"

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:40.250
That's just like you, huh?

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:43.240
BAM!

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:45.940
This place's inarizushi is great!

00:10:45.940 --> 00:10:47.630
And I got <i>this</i> too!

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:50.500
Ta-daa! A birthday cake!

00:10:52.090 --> 00:10:57.090
You got activated today,
so that makes it your birthday, right?

00:10:57.420 --> 00:11:01.650
Today... April 18th is my birthday.

00:11:01.650 --> 00:11:04.260
The birthday you chose for me.

00:11:04.400 --> 00:11:06.020
Happy birthday!

00:11:11.240 --> 00:11:15.410
Uh, do Frame Arm Girls not eat?

00:11:15.410 --> 00:11:16.330
Correct.

00:11:16.330 --> 00:11:18.490
Ah. Well, that's a shame.

00:11:18.790 --> 00:11:23.880
No... I think there is no shame in this feeling.

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:26.090
Oh, really?

00:11:26.090 --> 00:11:30.130
Yes. However, I do not know what to call this emotion.

00:11:30.840 --> 00:11:32.290
Don't worry about that.

00:11:34.090 --> 00:11:37.050
You'll figure it out, right? With that AS of yours.

00:11:40.020 --> 00:11:41.350
That's true.

00:11:43.260 --> 00:11:46.970
Stylet and Baselard

00:11:57.530 --> 00:11:59.190
Have a good day, Ao.

00:11:59.190 --> 00:12:01.040
Okay, see you later.

00:12:04.180 --> 00:12:05.360
I knew it...

00:12:05.360 --> 00:12:06.950
And <i>two</i> of them?

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:11.590
I get the feeling it'd be a hassle to open them now,
so I'll do it when I'm back from school.

00:12:11.590 --> 00:12:13.720
I'll be counting on you in case anything happens, Gourai.

00:12:13.720 --> 00:12:14.720
Understood, Ao.

00:12:14.720 --> 00:12:15.460
See you.

00:12:18.760 --> 00:12:20.770
I've found you, Gourai!

00:12:26.440 --> 00:12:28.110
Not bad.

00:12:29.730 --> 00:12:31.360
Who's this? A friend?

00:12:31.360 --> 00:12:33.810
I wouldn't call her a friend...

00:12:34.570 --> 00:12:36.060
I'm Stylet.

00:12:36.060 --> 00:12:39.980
Stylet? Another gift from Papa?

00:12:39.980 --> 00:12:42.200
Gennai Ao: are you an idiot?

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:45.460
An idiot? Idiot? You're dissing me?!

00:12:45.620 --> 00:12:48.130
Gourai, hurry and get ready.

00:12:48.130 --> 00:12:49.460
Let's battle.

00:12:49.460 --> 00:12:50.500
"Battle"?

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:53.010
It means we're going to fight. Probably.

00:12:53.510 --> 00:12:56.260
But why would you fight? I don't get it.

00:12:56.260 --> 00:12:59.890
You two! There's no how or why about it!

00:12:59.890 --> 00:13:04.520
Battling was the whole reason we were sent here, you giant idiots!

00:13:04.520 --> 00:13:05.510
"Giant" idiots?!

00:13:05.510 --> 00:13:07.850
You said "we" just now, didn't you?

00:13:07.850 --> 00:13:10.560
So then, a Frame Arms Girl is in here as well?

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:12.230
Well, of course!

00:13:12.230 --> 00:13:13.820
What? There's another one?

00:13:13.820 --> 00:13:15.400
Why hasn't she come out?

00:13:15.400 --> 00:13:18.000
I don't know. She's probably asleep.

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:18.840
F.A. Girl!

00:13:22.790 --> 00:13:24.200
Whoa. She really <i>is</i> asleep!

00:13:24.200 --> 00:13:25.160
Indeed.

00:13:25.160 --> 00:13:27.830
Wake up, Baselard!

00:13:47.140 --> 00:13:48.930
Don't fall back asleep!

00:13:52.770 --> 00:13:54.030
Ouch...

00:13:54.480 --> 00:13:58.850
Cut that out, Stylet! I'm still sleepy!

00:14:00.570 --> 00:14:02.580
Nice to meet you, Baselard.

00:14:02.580 --> 00:14:04.240
Ah, Gourai!

00:14:04.240 --> 00:14:06.830
So you got activated, huh?

00:14:06.830 --> 00:14:08.360
Awesome! Awesome!

00:14:08.620 --> 00:14:12.410
So, so, how'd the battle go? Who won?

00:14:14.840 --> 00:14:16.380
We haven't done it yet.

00:14:16.380 --> 00:14:16.910
Huh?

00:14:16.910 --> 00:14:19.430
Why're you wasting time, Stylet?!

00:14:19.430 --> 00:14:21.340
You're not one to talk, sleepyhead!

00:14:21.340 --> 00:14:22.140
Um...

00:14:22.800 --> 00:14:24.760
Why are you two here?

00:14:24.760 --> 00:14:27.230
And what do you mean about fighting me?

00:14:29.580 --> 00:14:33.680
Did neither of you read the e-mail from Factory Advance?

00:14:36.070 --> 00:14:37.440
Oh, there it is.

00:14:37.440 --> 00:14:40.070
It was in my Spam folder!

00:14:41.410 --> 00:14:42.980
Uh...

00:14:42.980 --> 00:14:44.980
"Gennai Ao-sama,
Re: Receipt of F.A. Girls
To: Me
From: Factory Advance

00:14:44.980 --> 00:14:47.830
this is in regards to Gourai, the Frame Arms Girl currently under development at our company.

00:14:47.830 --> 00:14:49.120
Re: Receipt of F.A. Girls

00:14:49.120 --> 00:14:53.920
this is in regards to Gourai, the Frame Arms Girl currently under development at our company.

00:14:53.920 --> 00:14:58.710
Please accept our apologies for this inconvenience, but..."

00:14:58.920 --> 00:15:00.960
Ao? What is it?

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:03.550
This e-mail's too long.
I can't be bothered to read it.

00:15:03.550 --> 00:15:04.590
So, what's going on?

00:15:04.590 --> 00:15:09.680
Well, they sent Gourai test models out to a bunch of different people,

00:15:09.680 --> 00:15:14.220
but yours is the only one that's been activated.

00:15:14.220 --> 00:15:15.770
Oh, really?

00:15:15.770 --> 00:15:18.390
I just kinda pushed stuff at random...

00:15:18.530 --> 00:15:21.780
That randomness led to a miracle!

00:15:21.780 --> 00:15:26.650
This is the only active Gourai in the world,
so Factory Advance is paying close attention.

00:15:26.910 --> 00:15:30.200
Now I see. That's why I have to be battle tested?

00:15:30.200 --> 00:15:33.040
But what's the point of fighting?

00:15:33.290 --> 00:15:35.720
The battle data will be collected and analyzed

00:15:35.720 --> 00:15:40.300
so Frame Arms Girls can be installed with a more advanced AS.

00:15:40.300 --> 00:15:45.630
If they want to mass produce a good product, they've gotta collect a lot of data!

00:15:47.640 --> 00:15:49.510
So you guys are like free samples!

00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:50.770
Yup, that's right!

00:15:51.600 --> 00:15:53.650
This is making my head hurt...

00:15:54.270 --> 00:15:55.310
Baselard.

00:15:55.310 --> 00:15:55.860
Hm?

00:15:55.860 --> 00:15:58.070
Sorry, but I'd like to battle her first.

00:15:58.070 --> 00:15:59.650
I want to win this and go home.

00:15:59.650 --> 00:16:00.640
Gotcha!

00:16:01.440 --> 00:16:03.020
You think you can beat me?

00:16:03.610 --> 00:16:04.900
Of course.

00:16:05.240 --> 00:16:06.830
Okay, so let's battle.

00:16:06.830 --> 00:16:08.280
Wait, hold on!

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:10.200
You're doing this battle thing <i>here?!</i>

00:16:10.200 --> 00:16:11.740
Not so much "here" as...

00:16:12.580 --> 00:16:15.490
In this Session Base!

00:16:32.980 --> 00:16:36.930
Hey, Gourai? If Stylet wins, battle me next, okay?

00:16:38.150 --> 00:16:41.180
Ao. Would you please attach my armor?

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:42.570
Huh? But how?

00:16:42.570 --> 00:16:45.570
An app should have been attached to that prior e-mail.

00:16:46.440 --> 00:16:48.440
Oh, yeah. This, right?

00:16:49.200 --> 00:16:52.700
Place Shoulder Armor on my left shoulder and the smoothbore on my right.

00:16:52.700 --> 00:16:57.580
Then, put Knee Armor over my Thigh Armor and treads behind my Leg Armor.

00:16:57.580 --> 00:17:01.200
And please place the Tactical Knife alongside my left Leg Armor.

00:17:03.340 --> 00:17:06.080
Gourai? You ready to lose?

00:17:08.390 --> 00:17:09.050
Gourai...

00:17:09.050 --> 00:17:09.920
Stylet...

00:17:10.390 --> 00:17:12.720
Frame Arms Girl Session...

00:17:12.720 --> 00:17:13.840
Go!
Just you watch!

00:17:26.650 --> 00:17:28.940
This moment, right now...

00:17:28.940 --> 00:17:30.120
is a party!

00:17:37.620 --> 00:17:40.130
Well then... here I go!

00:17:47.380 --> 00:17:48.640
Where is Stylet?

00:17:55.350 --> 00:17:57.840
Oh, wow! Stylet sure is fast!

00:18:02.770 --> 00:18:04.470
What are you aiming at?

00:18:04.470 --> 00:18:05.900
I can't reach her.

00:18:06.190 --> 00:18:07.480
This is...

00:18:13.940 --> 00:18:17.910
Oh, dear. It looks like Gourai's smoothbore has a straggler.

00:18:17.910 --> 00:18:18.950
"Straggler"?

00:18:19.710 --> 00:18:24.200
A piece left behind when the parts are removed from the runner.

00:18:24.380 --> 00:18:28.220
Her parts aren't on tight, so she can't aim properly.

00:18:28.220 --> 00:18:28.970
Tee-hee!

00:18:28.970 --> 00:18:30.970
What are you doing? You're hopeless!

00:18:30.970 --> 00:18:34.060
You mean, I might not have cut it out properly?

00:18:34.060 --> 00:18:35.180
That's right!

00:18:35.970 --> 00:18:37.600
I'm sorry, Gourai!

00:18:42.280 --> 00:18:43.430
Piece of cake.

00:18:43.430 --> 00:18:44.940
I get it.

00:18:44.940 --> 00:18:48.270
The smoothbore was loose, so you forced it on, huh?

00:18:48.270 --> 00:18:50.260
Still, why can't she hit her?

00:18:50.260 --> 00:18:55.220
Gourai's smoothbore never had a chance against Stylet.

00:18:55.220 --> 00:18:57.000
I mean, Stylet's fast, and she's flying!

00:18:57.000 --> 00:18:59.820
So she's had a disadvantage right from the start!

00:18:59.820 --> 00:19:04.580
Yup! But I want the data on how Gourai plans to fight her.

00:19:06.000 --> 00:19:07.760
So that's it...

00:19:07.760 --> 00:19:08.750
Gourai!

00:19:08.750 --> 00:19:09.340
Yes.

00:19:09.340 --> 00:19:11.680
This one here said your shots will land if you get closer.

00:19:11.680 --> 00:19:12.500
But...

00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:14.500
Why don't <i>you</i> fly too?

00:19:19.220 --> 00:19:20.840
Understood, Ao!

00:19:22.900 --> 00:19:24.650
You're just gonna ram me?

00:19:24.650 --> 00:19:25.970
Talk about desperate.

00:19:35.120 --> 00:19:37.150
Are you ready to lose?

00:19:47.000 --> 00:19:48.910
Winner: Gourai!

00:19:53.400 --> 00:19:55.130
Whoa! You won, Gourai!

00:19:55.620 --> 00:19:56.850
Thanks to you, Ao.

00:19:56.850 --> 00:19:57.880
Me?

00:19:58.920 --> 00:19:59.880
Yes.

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:02.520
I-It can't be... I lost?

00:20:02.520 --> 00:20:03.480
Stylet!

00:20:04.600 --> 00:20:06.930
You were super cool yourself!

00:20:07.940 --> 00:20:09.850
I-I was "cool"?

00:20:10.030 --> 00:20:10.860
Yup!

00:20:11.820 --> 00:20:15.620
Oh, my. Are you blushing?
You blushing there, Stylet?

00:20:16.120 --> 00:20:17.480
Of course I'm not!

00:20:17.480 --> 00:20:20.280
Next time, I'll beat you for sure, Gourai!

00:20:20.280 --> 00:20:21.790
Huh? You're going to do that <i>again?</i>

00:20:21.790 --> 00:20:23.210
Well, of course!

00:20:23.210 --> 00:20:25.040
I can't let this end with a loss!

00:20:27.040 --> 00:20:29.560
You do hate losing, don't you?

00:20:29.560 --> 00:20:31.750
Rather, she has an inflated sense of pride.

00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:34.510
It was interesting watching you two battle...

00:20:34.510 --> 00:20:37.800
Still, watching this go on and on could get old quick.

00:20:37.800 --> 00:20:38.540
Ao!

00:20:39.380 --> 00:20:44.270
If you help us gather battle data,
Factory Advance will pay you for it.

00:20:44.270 --> 00:20:46.470
Huh? Really?! How much?

00:20:46.470 --> 00:20:49.390
It should be more than you could get working part-time.

00:20:49.390 --> 00:20:50.480
For real?!

00:20:50.480 --> 00:20:54.150
Yes! I was thinking I'd probably have to get a job!

00:20:54.150 --> 00:20:55.900
I'll do it! I'll totally do it!

00:20:56.160 --> 00:20:59.150
Speaking of, do you not have to go to school today?

00:21:01.540 --> 00:21:04.210
Oh, no! I'm gonna be late for sure!

00:21:04.210 --> 00:21:05.710
This is bad! Bad! BAD!

00:21:05.710 --> 00:21:08.130
See you later!

00:21:10.500 --> 00:21:14.100
They'll soon show up at your door,

00:21:14.100 --> 00:21:19.500
for my special someone, parts of hearts!

00:21:24.140 --> 00:21:29.780
Counting the days I can't see you,

00:21:30.970 --> 00:21:37.230
I want to hear your voice so badly I feel like crying!

00:21:37.230 --> 00:21:40.720
I'm new to this world,

00:21:40.720 --> 00:21:44.190
so I lack the language to describe it.

00:21:44.190 --> 00:21:46.460
To knockoffs, say...

00:21:46.460 --> 00:21:49.910
"No!" Take care to avoid them.

00:21:49.910 --> 00:21:53.430
I want to be be dedicated!

00:21:56.820 --> 00:22:02.130
I want to build it all from nothing!

00:22:02.130 --> 00:22:05.360
We laugh and we fight,

00:22:05.360 --> 00:22:08.970
creating our unique specs!

00:22:08.970 --> 00:22:14.890
By mixing love and hate,

00:22:14.890 --> 00:22:23.000
I want to create more of these funny, carefree days, the parts of Girl!

00:22:40.340 --> 00:22:43.390
Gourai, you know, I can see your butt...

00:22:43.390 --> 00:22:44.560
It's a bodysuit.

00:22:44.560 --> 00:22:46.270
Huh? But that-

00:22:46.270 --> 00:22:47.770
It's a bodysuit.

00:22:48.020 --> 00:22:51.200
Next time, on Frame Arms Girl... All together now.

00:22:51.200 --> 00:22:52.100
Session!

00:22:52.100 --> 00:22:52.480
I'm Gonna Clean!

00:22:52.480 --> 00:22:54.160
But you wear panties, don't you?

00:22:54.160 --> 00:22:54.970
I'm Gonna Clean!
